# Security headers - Server-level enforcement reference.
# GitHub Pages does not natively support custom HTTP headers.
# To enforce these, use a CDN/proxy like Cloudflare in front of GitHub Pages,
# or migrate to a platform that supports _headers (e.g., Netlify, Vercel).
# This file serves as documentation of the desired security headers.
#
# NOTE on CSP: 'unsafe-inline' for style-src is required while inline styles
# are used across the site. To eliminate it, extract all inline styles to
# external CSS files and use nonce or hash-based CSP instead.
# 'unsafe-inline' for script-src has been removed — all inline scripts should
# be moved to external .js files, or use nonce-based CSP at the server level.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'


